"""aichat runs bin/<tool> '<json arguments>' with LLM_OUTPUT set to a file it
reads the result from (the llm-functions layout, see functions.json). Every
bin/<tool> is a link to this script, which picks the tool by its own name. It
runs only when that name is in MASCOT_TOOLS_ALLOWED, the tools the bubble chose.

Nothing here writes or deletes anything but the todo list and the reminders,
Mascot's own MASCOT_TODO_FILE and MASCOT_REMINDER_FILE. The file tools only see
the home directory, and no hidden files or directories but the ones the user
let them see (CHAT_DOTFILES, passed as MASCOT_DOTFILES). Even there, never where
secrets are kept (SECRET_DIRS and SECRET_NAMES: .ssh, keys, tokens, browser
profiles, shell history...). The file, todo and reminder tools only work when the bubble
says the model is local (MASCOT_TOOLS_LOCAL=1), so what they read stays on this
computer. So does last_commands, the one tool that reads shell history: only
its last commands, and never one that looks like it holds a secret. And so do
check_system and read_log, which read what the system's own tools and log say
(nmcli, ss, UFW's rules, wpctl, coredumpctl, systemctl, journalctl), never
with sudo, with what looks like a password or key in a log line hidden."""

